## Summary
The first GDPR fine in Italy was imposed on Rousseau, an online voter consultation platform used by the 5 Star Movement, for €50,000 due to data security vulnerabilities. This case sets a precedent for data processor liabilities under GDPR and emphasizes the need for strong data protection in online platforms.

## Key Points
- Italy issued its first-ever GDPR fine targeting data security liabilities.
- Rousseau was fined €50,000 for leaving user data vulnerable to attackers.
- The fine clarifies the responsibilities of data processors under GDPR.
- The case involves a political party's platform, demonstrating GDPR's broad applicability.


